{"items":[{"owner":{"account_id":9856,"reputation":595,"user_id":117057,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/27E99.png?s=256","display_name":"shoover","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/117057/shoover"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1551307125,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":6447221,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"OP, what did you end up getting the FRS, and how did it work out?"},{"owner":{"account_id":6498539,"reputation":4276,"user_id":249419,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":80,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/CCmKh.jpg?s=256","display_name":"Prince M","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/249419/prince-m"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526705658,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5747545,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Men of Math by ET Bell"},{"owner":{"account_id":431507,"reputation":29242,"user_id":30481,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":62,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/aff0866587273eeae903c6bd2715b717?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Jack M","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/30481/jack-m"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1526580388,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5743823,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Does he have a particular interest in history? Being a professor of mathematics doesn&#39;t necessarily make you an expert in the history of mathematics."},{"owner":{"account_id":383876,"reputation":153943,"user_id":1551,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":83,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/AJuVVoi8.png?s=256","display_name":"user1551","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/1551/user1551"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1526555732,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5742920,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"If he is not well, you&#39;d better pick a book that is easy to hold, not too heavy and in large print. And perhaps it doesn&#39;t have to be a book on mathematical history. Other expositions on arts or science may do just fine."},{"owner":{"account_id":3572634,"reputation":102197,"user_id":108274,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":94,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/4fc987e57b8626e201e75450a705047e?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Mauro ALLEGRANZA","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/108274/mauro-allegranza"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526539364,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5742502,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Springer has a full series dedicated to the <a href=\"https://www.springer.com/series/4142?detailsPage=titles\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">History of Mathematics and Physical Sciences</a> (not divulgative)."},{"owner":{"account_id":8361663,"reputation":6868,"user_id":347062,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":48,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/S5jqZ.jpg?s=256","display_name":"gen-ℤ ready to perish","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/347062/gen-%e2%84%a4-ready-to-perish"},"edited":false,"score":12,"creation_date":1526523469,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5742170,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"At first glance of your title I thought you were being grandiose, but then I read the question body, and I have to say, <b>your thoughtfulness really warms my heart. I’m sure any book you deliver to him will lift his spirits, just because it shows you care.</b> I wish you the best of luck $\\ddot\\smile$"},{"owner":{"account_id":3475378,"reputation":416,"user_id":209104,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/1xBJR.png?s=256","display_name":"bishop","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/209104/bishop"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526517274,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5742032,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Provided he&#39;s not the one and same, perhaps your ailing friend might enjoy an engaging light read by a fellow Professor and FRS: Ian Stewart&#39;s, <a href=\"https://rads.stackoverflow.com/amzn/click/com/0262534282\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\"><i>The Beauty of Numbers</i></a> or any of his <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ian_Stewart_(mathematician)#Mathematics_and_popular_science\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">other fine works</a>."},{"owner":{"account_id":510256,"reputation":411750,"user_id":622,"user_type":"moderator","accept_rate":87,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/8592b8e3b742e752b7b50d9ef1029931?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Asaf Karagila","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/622/asaf-karagila"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":5751779,"reputation":5301,"user_id":283224,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":100,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/a71748eb4f7bc1d460f54a86a95f58f5?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Kevin Long","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/283224/kevin-long"},"edited":false,"score":4,"creation_date":1526502172,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5741597,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Kevin: Unfortunately, I think that getting Erdős to help is impossible nowadays."},{"owner":{"account_id":5751779,"reputation":5301,"user_id":283224,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":100,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/a71748eb4f7bc1d460f54a86a95f58f5?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Kevin Long","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/283224/kevin-long"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":511689,"reputation":149922,"user_id":10400,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":67,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/9d36c6c0fe72160847d8aff404d9f1a0?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Will Jagy","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/10400/will-jagy"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526498922,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5741454,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@WillJagy Hopefully this isn&#39;t getting too off topic, but I&#39;ve heard that when Stan Ulam was in the hospital for encephalitis, Paul Erdos went to meet him when he was discharged and spent a few weeks at his house, plying him with math questions and playing chess with him. At the time, Ulam was afraid that the incident would have affected his mathematical ability, but Erdos helped him build his confidence back up. So if the professor in question is feeling suboptimal, some (small) math problems might be good."},{"owner":{"account_id":510256,"reputation":411750,"user_id":622,"user_type":"moderator","accept_rate":87,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/8592b8e3b742e752b7b50d9ef1029931?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Asaf Karagila","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/622/asaf-karagila"},"edited":false,"score":6,"creation_date":1526493792,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5741224,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"It would be helpful if you know the field of interest of this Fellow, then we can recommend a book that might be more or less of interest to them."},{"owner":{"account_id":1446758,"reputation":8277,"user_id":30261,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":82,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/Mejba.jpg?s=256","display_name":"Fixed Point","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/30261/fixed-point"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526492605,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5741159,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Undergraduate/Graduate level books don&#39;t have to be patronizing. I am sure there are some mathematical fields in which he is not an expert but he has always wanted to learn more about. He might be very happy with an undergrad/grad level book in those topics. I don&#39;t know if you can ask him or any of his colleagues/friends/family. But I, for sure, would be very delighted receiving such a gift. In fact, not just math, but there may be plenty of other types of books (fiction/nonfiction) like scifi, mythologies, Freud, or WWII history books which he would truly appreciate."},{"owner":{"account_id":510331,"reputation":55983,"user_id":1242,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/e57993275f5c6275936a449aece862ba?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Hans Lundmark","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/1242/hans-lundmark"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526488844,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5741014,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"You may get some ideas from this thread: <a href=\"https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/2436947/mathematical-math-history-books\" title=\"mathematical math history books\">math.stackexchange.com/questions/2436947/&hellip;</a>. I can repeat my recommendation made there of Hawkins&#39;s books."},{"owner":{"account_id":5211826,"reputation":999,"user_id":439987,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/GQIrI.jpg?s=256","display_name":"Kino","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/439987/kino"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1526487797,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5740954,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Yes, sorry, FRS is Fellow of the Royal Society. I&#39;ll add that to the main post."},{"owner":{"account_id":1832322,"reputation":13645,"user_id":79043,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":100,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/gqrRp.png?s=256","display_name":"mathematics2x2life","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/79043/mathematics2x2life"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1526486437,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5740889,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I am not so sure such a thing exists. However if you know his area of mathematics, you can find plenty of biographies of mathematicians is most any given field that detail their life and mathematics at very advanced levels. Perhaps that might be closer to what you wanted?"},{"owner":{"account_id":3572634,"reputation":102197,"user_id":108274,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":94,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/4fc987e57b8626e201e75450a705047e?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Mauro ALLEGRANZA","link":"https://math.stackexchange.com/users/108274/mauro-allegranza"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1526486128,"post_id":2783869,"comment_id":5740879,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Not a single book encompassing &quot;all&quot; history of math... Some recent suggestions : Jeremy Gray, <a href=\"https://books.google.it/books?id=zpDDCgAAQBAJ&amp;printsec=frontcover\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">The Real and the Complex : A History of Analysis in the 19th Century</a>, Springer (2015) and Thomas Sonar, <a href=\"https://books.google.it/books?id=NJJVDwAAQBAJ&amp;printsec=frontcover\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">The History of the Priority Dispute between Newton and Leibniz</a> (2018, Birkh&#228;user)."}],"has_more":false,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":288}